## 1. Exact local coefficient spaces

For an oriented nine-cycle family, write the two exact rational quotient-coordinate rows at touched block `b` as `x_b,y_b` in `Q^9`. The actual-empty coefficient space is

`E_b = span{x_b,y_b}`.

The three possible singleton coefficient lines are obtained from the three local root-row directions

`(1,0), (0,1), (1,-1)`

by taking the exact normal row

`l_x y_b - l_y x_b`.

This is the same local construction used by the earlier repository `block_profile` verifiers. A zero normal is retained as a legitimate zero singleton constraint.

For the support above, the two multiplicity-three supports contain all three orientations, while each of the other three supports chooses one of three orientations. Hence there are exactly

`3^3 = 27`

oriented nine-cycle families.

## 2. Superset enumeration of aggregate four-spaces

Let `W` be the aggregate coefficient-constraint rowspace. Since the external coefficient code `P` has dimension five in nine coordinates, every actual state has

`dim W = 4`, `P = ker W`.

In the two-singleton profile, `W` is generated by all actual-empty spaces together with at most two nonzero singleton lines; a selected singleton may contribute the zero line. The verifier therefore enumerates every rank-four rowspace generated by

- an arbitrary subset of the touched `E_b`, and
- at most two arbitrary nonzero singleton lines from touched blocks.

It deliberately permits incompatible choices, repeated-source patterns, and choices that do not correspond to a legal root-state assignment. This only enlarges the search. Every realizable two-singleton state is represented.

The committed nine-coordinate parity-check lemma is then applied exactly. For a full-row-rank `4 x 9` matrix with rowspace `W`, the required generalized weights

`(d1,d2,d3,d4,d5)(ker W) >= (2,4,5,7,8)`

are equivalent to:

1. no zero column;
2. every three columns have rank at least two;
3. every six columns have rank at least three.

All ranks in this verifier use exact rational arithmetic.

## 3. Structural relaxation

For a candidate `W`, define the virtual-incomplete touched family `V(W)` to contain every touched block `b` for which either

- `E_b <= W`, or
- at least one of the three singleton constraints at `b` is zero or is a subspace of `W`.

For any actual state producing `W`, every actual touched incomplete block lies in `V(W)`: actual-empty blocks satisfy the first condition, and selected-singleton blocks satisfy the second. Therefore

`C* = T \ V(W)`

is a subset of the actual touched complete family `C`.

Because `d_root=0`, the triangle rows of `C` are independent, so the rows of `C*` must also be independent. The four external relation directions give

`rank H(T) - rank H(C) >= 4`.

Since `C*` is a subset of `C`,

`rank H(T) - rank H(C*) >= rank H(T) - rank H(C) >= 4`.

Thus both structural tests used by the verifier are necessary for every actual state. The virtual-incomplete construction is intentionally larger than the actual incomplete family, so this gate cannot exclude a realizable state merely by assigning extra virtual-incomplete blocks.

## 4. Executed exact census

The exact persisted source was syntax-checked and executed. It reproduces the following fail-closed census:

- oriented cycle families: `27`;
- relaxed rank-four aggregate spaces: `36,516`;
- generalized-weight-admissible spaces: `702`;
- rejected because `H(C*)` is dependent: `318`;
- rejected because `rank H(T)-rank H(C*) < 4`: `384`;
- structural survivors: `0`.

The two rejection counts partition all 702 generalized-weight-admissible spaces.

## 5. Result

The support orbit

`[0123]^3 [0124]^3 [0134] [0234] [1234]`

has no realizable state in the two-selected-singleton profile.

The earlier support-level computation left 13 two-singleton support orbits. This certificate removes this explicit orbit from the unresolved set. The remaining support orbits still require repository-audited orientation certificates; previous non-persisted zero-survivor evidence for other representatives is not promoted by this note.
